'''''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]''''' returned for its '''twentieth series''' with a launch show on 23 September 2022 on BBC One, with live shows beginning the following day on 24 September.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/schedules/p00fzl6p/2022/09/24 | title=BBC One London – Schedules, Saturday 24 September 2022 }}</ref> The launch show was originally scheduled to be broadcast on 17 September, but was postponed following the [[death of Queen Elizabeth II]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing postponed after death of the Queen |url=https://theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2022/sep/13/strictly-come-dancing-postponed-after-death-of-the-queen |website=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=23 September 2022 |date=23 September 2022}}</ref> [[Tess Daly]] and [[Claudia Winkleman]] returned as hosts, while [[Rylan Clark]] and [[Janette Manrara]] returned to host ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]].''<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.essexlive.news/news/celebs-tv/strictly-come-dancing-2022-start-7440856|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2022: start date, line-up and judges|website=[[Essex Chronicle]]|first=Sophie|last=Christian|date=9 August 2022|accessdate=9 August 2022|language=en-GB}}</ref>

In May 2022, the BBC announced that [[Shirley Ballas]], [[Anton Du Beke]], [[Motsi Mabuse]], and [[Craig Revel Horwood]] would return to the judging panel.<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 May 2022 |title=Judges revealed for 2022 series of Strictly Come Dancing |url= https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2022/strictly-judges-2022 | website=[[BBC]]}}</ref> It was also confirmed that [[Bruno Tonioli]], who had been absent from the two previous series due to travel restrictions resulting from the [[COVID-19 pandemic]], would be permanently leaving the show.<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 May 2022 |title=Bruno Tonioli leaves Strictly Come Dancing for good |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-61491630 |website=[[BBC News]]}}</ref>

In August 2022, the BBC confirmed that the show would return to the [[Blackpool Tower Ballroom]] for the first time since the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 17|seventeenth series]].<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/newsround/62623704 |title=Strictly Come Dancing: Show returns to Blackpool with new BBC-themed week – CBBC Newsround |publisher=[[BBC News]] |accessdate=23 September 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.itv.com/news/2022-08-21/strictly-come-dancing-2022-blackpool-return-and-themed-week-for-bbc-centenary |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2022: Blackpool return and themed week for BBC centenary &#124; ITV News |publisher=[[ITV News]]|date= 21 August 2022|accessdate=23 September 2022}}</ref> It was also announced that there would be a special themed week to celebrate the 100th anniversary of the [[BBC]], with the couples dancing to "a theme tune from an iconic BBC programme or in tribute to one of the BBC's most loved services".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2022/aug/22/strictly-come-dancing-bbc-centenary-blackpool-tower-ballroom |title=Strictly Come Dancing to celebrate BBC centenary with themed week &#124; Strictly Come Dancing |work=The Guardian |date=2018-01-31 |accessdate=23 September 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a40956437/strictly-come-dancing-2022-bbc-100-theme/ |title=Strictly 2022 confirms one-off special for BBC's 100th birthday |publisher=[[Digital Spy]] |date= 22 August 2022|accessdate=23 September 2022}}</ref>

[[Wildlife]] presenter [[Hamza Yassin]] and [[Jowita Przystał]] were announced as the winners on 17 December,<ref>{{cite web |last=Saunders |first=Emma |date=17 December 2022 |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2022: Hamza Yassin wins glitterball trophy |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-63943808 |access-date=18 December 2022 |publisher=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> while singer-songwriter [[Fleur East]] and [[Vito Coppola]], ''[[Nova Jones]]'' actress [[Molly Rainford]] and [[Carlos Gu]], and television presenter [[Helen Skelton]] and [[Gorka Márquez]] were the runners-up.

