The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. The couples are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the lowest scored couple receiving one point, and the highest scored couple receiving the most points (the maximum number of points available depends on the number of couples remaining in the competition). The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; the couple with the fewest votes receiving one point, and the couple with the most votes receiving the most points.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Shirley Ballas]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]].

== Professional dancers ==
On 22 February 2022, it was announced that [[Oti Mabuse]] was leaving the series after seven years,<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 February 2022 |title=Oti Mabuse to leave Strictly Come Dancing after seven years |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-60476377|website=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> and on 28 March 2022, that [[Aljaž Škorjanec]] was also leaving after nine years (He returned to the show in 2024).<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 March 2022 |title=Aljaž Škorjanec is leaving Strictly Come Dancing |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-60899783|website=[[BBC News]]}}</ref> Three days after Škorjanec's departure, the BBC announced that the rest of the current professionals would be returning to the series.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2022 |title=Professional dancers returning for Strictly Come Dancing Series 20 confirmed |url=https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2022/strictly-professional-dancers-returning-for-series-20 |website=[[BBC]]}}</ref>

In July 2022, the BBC announced that four new professional dancers would be joining the cast: European cup winner [[Vito Coppola]], who was also a professional dancer on the [[Ballando con le Stelle|Italian version of the show]] in 2021; Chinese National Champion [[Carlos Gu]]; former Under 21 British National Champion Lauren Oakley; and Latin dance champion Michelle Tsiakkas.<ref>{{Cite web |date=11 July 2022 |title=Four new pros join the show in 2022! |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/a8605a54-777e-4688-a243-e562124abee3 |website=[[BBC]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=11 July 2022 |title=Strictly Come Dancing reveals new professionals joining for 2022 |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-new-professionals-2022-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]]}}</ref> [[Jowita Przystał]] received a celebrity partner for the first time, as did new professionals [[Vito Coppola]] and [[Carlos Gu]]; while [[Neil Jones (dancer)|Neil Jones]], [[Cameron Lombard]], [[Luba Mushtuk]], [[Lauren Oakley]], and [[Michelle Tsiakkas]] did not receive a partner.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Jones |first1=Gemma |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2022: Full list of pairings and professionals without partners |url=https://www.liverpoolecho.co.uk/news/tv/strictly-come-dancing-2022-full-25096629 |website=[[Liverpool Echo]] |access-date=15 October 2022 |date=23 September 2022}}</ref>

==Couples==
This series featured fifteen celebrity contestants. On 4 August 2022, the first two celebrities announced were [[Will Mellor]] and [[Kym Marsh]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/5ca60ca4-a8ba-46af-991f-927f4f609009|title=Will Mellor is the first celebrity contestant confirmed for Strictly Come Dancing 2022!|date=4 August 2022 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/41ad83aa-ca43-4b73-91ca-29cba20bce50|title=Kym Marsh is the second celebrity contestant confirmed for 2022!| date=4 August 2022 }}</ref> Celebrity contestants continued to be revealed until 13 August 2022, when the full line-up was announced.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.dailypost.co.uk/news/tv/strictly-come-dancing-full-line-24740012|title=Strictly Come Dancing: The full line-up including soap stars and Loose Women host|website=[[Daily Post (North Wales)|Daily Post]]|first=Alex|last=Whilding|date=13 August 2022|accessdate=13 August 2022|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.edinburghnews.scotsman.com/read-this/strictly-come-dancing-2022-pairings-full-list-of-couples-for-the-new-series-and-how-to-watch-bbc-one-show-3855318|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2022 pairings: Full list of couples for the new series – and how to watch BBC One show|website=[[Edinburgh Evening News]]|first=Ethan|last=Evans|date=24 September 2022|accessdate=24 September 2022|language=en-GB}}</ref> During the results show on 13 November, after initially being announced as one of the bottom two couples, [[Tony Adams]] and [[Katya Jones]] withdrew from the competition due to Adams having sustained a [[hamstring]] injury during their original performance.<ref name=":0">{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing: Tony Adams withdraws with an injury |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-63615618 |website=[[BBC]] |access-date=23 November 2022 |date=13 November 2022}}</ref>
